### 2.3 Construction choice
**Layered inline SVG inside one HTML stage, driven by a pure `stateAt(cfg,t)` + `render(cfg,t)` (DOM/SVG), CONFIG at top.** Draw-on = stroke-dashoffset progress per layer group; type-on = character-count reveal from CONFIG strings; figures = one parameterized `<g>` icon (head circle + body path + chest glyph) instantiated for the magnifier figure (large, star glyph) and all array icons (small, plus glyph), selected icon gets ring + connectors.
Rejected: canvas particle system (no particle mechanic; would import A5 machinery with no subject) · CSS keyframes (timings would live in CSS literals, unswappable by CONFIG and unprobeable by the node harness) · traced frame sequence / specimen imagery (refusal class, §6.1) · generated imagery (the line-icon system is exact vector geometry; raster would blur the one-line-weight claim).

### 2.4 Swap values (exact)
- Content: texts.formula "P(F|H) ≈ 0.98" → "P(S|R) ≈ 0.87" · texts.slotWord "hope" → "luck" · texts.expansion[0] → "P(S|R) = P(R|S)·P(S) / Σᵢ P(R|Aᵢ)·P(Aᵢ) = (0.91 × 0.402) / 0.4205" · array.cols 10 → 8 (count 40 → 32, count assertion re-fires).
- Timing: timing.expandLineDurMs 550 → 1000 (expandEndMs 3150 → 4450; CP instants derived from it move).
- Palette: palette.ink "#ffffff" → "#7fd4ff" (observed in render output).

### 2.5 Failure points (priced)
- Convergent freeze / intensity collapse: array at ink intensity would fight the magnifier — cured by construction (array=dim, expansion=faint, subject=ink).
- Phrase overlap analogue: layers must not pre-appear — stateAt clamps every layer's raw progress to [0,1] with starts chained; harness asserts strict layer order at boundary instants.
- Fitting limits: expansion L2 is the longest line (66 chars) — fit leg measures it; if it overflows the 720 stage it wraps/shrinks via CONFIG type.expansionPx only (no logic literal).
- Phone legibility (digest B-a): expansion at 24 px native = 12 px at 360 stage — above the ~11 px floor but tight; fit leg must MEASURE, and a HIT is cured by raising expansionPx, never by dropping a line.
- Render-proof limitation: no browser binary in this seat — logic-level harness + PIL fit measurement; comparison page is the render surface (PIXEL-UNVERIFIED carried to scores.md).
- Count assertion (A9.3): source count 40 (4×10 counted firsthand) vs built count cols×rows — harness prints both and halts on mismatch.

### 2.6 Execute checklist
1. Cut segment.mp4: source 0–13.5 s → artifact dir, re-encode h264+AAC, ffprobe + sha256 recorded.
2. Build recreation.html per §2.1/§2.3 (CONFIG at top, stateAt/render, window.__T241 exposed for harness).
3. Build comparison.html (labels: ORIGINAL — ensan.besham Hope = Failure (?) @ 0–13 s · RECREATION — T241, parameterized; one synchronized control set; phone stacking).
4. Self-verify (§5 legs 1–3) via harness-t241.js; file A6 legs; assemble A13 receipt index; fire jev-prewave.

### 2.7 Verify checklist (instruments named)
- Swap test: node harness-t241.js with swapped CONFIGs (§2.4 exact values) — state assertions + render-string checks.
- Purity: `grep -nE "segment\.mp4|source\.mp4|<video|<img|DffiIpmMAC3" recreation.html` → 0 specimen hits; asset inventory = recreation.html alone.
- Syntax: extract inline script → `node --check`. Seeded RNG: none needed (no randomness in construction) — census prints NOT-APPLICABLE with reason.
- A11 checkpoints CP0–CP8 (§2.2 instants, CONFIG-derived expressions) in harness, each with executable receipt; timing swap must move CP instants tied to expandLineDurMs.
- A6: fit-table.md (PIL, named stand-in font, every text element incl. formula + all 3 expansion lines + callout lines) · config-census.md (literal scan classified; every key incl. nested texts.expansion[]/array.* resolved to a site).
- jev-prewave after legs 1–3 + A6 + A13 index; five-lens Codex wave only on FIRE-WAVE.

## §2b — Gate dispositions
_To be filled as the four Phase A returns land (codex-observe · jev-observe-exit · codex-plan-review · jev-plan-exit), before any build script (A9.2)._


=== GUARDS COMMAND LIST ===
# Guards — recreation

## The judgment layer's home (owner's order, 2026-11-14 — 100% form)
Form: **In-job form.** This job's judging = the Codex scoring wave (its review type, defined in `codex-scoring-wave.md` in this directory) + the mechanical guards below + `jev-prewave.md`. The wave's execution may be shared tooling; the definitions are this job's own files.

## The commands (mechanical guards — callable, demonstrated)
1. Construction-purity grep — recreation.html must contain no reference to source media, frames, or tracing (pattern census over the file).
   Demonstrated: 2026-11-13, T15 attempt 1 (zero hits; Codex purity lens independently returned 100).
   Pattern precision (2026-11-17, Cycle 026 Condense — priced across T167 · T170 · T175 in one wave): an in-file fragment reference `url(#id)` (an SVG paint-server or clip definition inside the same file) is NOT a specimen reference; such hits are classified in the item's build record and never counted as purity hits. The refusal class is specimen media, source files, and tracing — the grep's specimen alternatives (`segment.mp4|source.mp4|<video|<img|1235931636`-form source ids) stay unmodified.
2. Swap test (parameterization proof) — headless harness loads the recreation with a swapped CONFIG phrase; target geometry must regenerate for the new words (a traced copy cannot).
   Demonstrated: 2026-11-13, T15 attempt 1, LOGIC level (node harness, stubbed canvas: 5,060 → 2,728 targets). Pixel-level render proof is NOT exercisable from this seat (no browser binary) — printed limitation, carried in scores.md; the comparison page is the render surface.
3. Syntax + determinism check — `node --check` on inline scripts; seeded-RNG presence census.
   Demonstrated: 2026-11-13, T15 attempt 1 (both scripts clean).
4. Scores arithmetic — recompute the wave average + min from the filed lens returns before scores.md prints a verdict.
   Demonstrated: 2026-11-13, T15 attempt 1 (68/82/100/64 → 78.5 recomputed at filing).
5. Segment binding — segment.mp4's timestamps/duration/ffprobe facts recorded against the packet's technique window before any build starts.
   Demonstrated: 2026-11-13, T15 attempt 1 (1:24–1:40 · 16.0 s · ffprobe-cited).
6. **Measured-fit leg** — `guard-measured-fit.md` in this directory. Per item, pre-wave: every subject text element carries a MEASURED fit row (post-fit ink bounds vs container at the 360 px stage, legibility floor ~11 px); a formula-claimed fit or a missing row is a HIT. Owns the "fit asserted, not measured" readability class (Waves 2–5, 10). **Built 2026-11-15 (HQ owed-checks charge); fires unconditionally at the pre-wave step from the next cycle; a wave record lacking a fit table for any item prints INCOMPLETE.** Verdict advisory; firing is not.
7. **Config-census leg (v3.1 codified)** — `guard-config-census.md` in this directory. Per item, pre-wave: all-literal scan with per-constant subject-shaping/structural classification + CONFIG key→application-site resolution (nested/array keys included) + CSS-variable setter check; unapplied keys and unset-variable references are HITs. Owns the config-incompleteness reusability class. **Built 2026-11-15 (HQ owed-checks charge); fires unconditionally at the pre-wave step from the next cycle; a wave record lacking a census for any item prints INCOMPLETE.** Verdict advisory; firing is not.

## Jev call definitions
- `jev-prewave.md` — judges a build record's readiness to spend a scoring wave. **Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle. A cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE.** (Designed 2026-11-14; attempt 1 predates it and ran under the §5 panel, which runs alongside.)
- `jev-observe-exit.md` — the Observe→Plan gate for a recreation wave (queue state priced · prior/family scores read · mechanics seen · variables extracted · flow-field model + Owner Cures 1–2 carried in working memory · consumer named). Call point: INSTRUCTION §1 gate out. **Firing: this call fires at its step on every cyc

