**T241 — REVISE · Primary classification `UNBOUND-SCHEDULE`**

At 1,000 ms, the census mapping says all 40 icons are complete. The CONFIG yields **16 complete icons**: `1 + floor((1000 − 600 − 180) / 14)`. The last icon completes at `600 + 39 × 14 + 180 = 1326 ms`, versus 1,150 ms in the sub-beat schedule. The Plan can clear this charge by aligning the sub-beat schedule and census mapping with the CONFIG, then recording the incomplete array at 1,000 ms as part of the deliberate opening departure. [T241 Plan, §§1.3, 2.1–2.2](item-T241-observe-plan.md#22-census-anchor-mapping-a102--departure-table)

