The census amendment also needs a 500 ms row: source L1 is near-complete while build L1 has yet to start. At 2,000 ms, L2 reveal progress is zero at its exact onset. At 3,000 ms, L3 is about 73% through its reveal while the census shows it landed. The Plan should align those cues or carry them explicitly as departures, and reconcile the prose’s ≈3.4 s L3 landing and 6.2 s dissolve endpoint with f-3 and f-6. The opening draw-on and T242 handoff are already declared departures. The census and filed Observe charges are sufficient to make these revisions in Plan. [T241 Plan, §§1.2, 2.1–2.7](item-T241-observe-plan.md) · [Filed Observe-exit](item-T241-jev-observe-exit-return.md)

